Third-party code

wry and tao (https://github.com/tauri-apps/wry, https://github.com/tauri-apps/tao)
  Dependencies of crates/host, under Apache-2.0 or MIT. The host's window and event loop follow
  wry's `simple` example.

BU Bench (https://github.com/browser-use/benchmark)
  benchmarks/bu-bench/misty_eval.py runs against a separate checkout of BU Bench and imports its
  code there (task loading, selection, the findings judge, scoring and summaries); none of that
  code is copied here. Its evidence layout and the task prompt follow BU Bench's BrowserCode
  runner. The BU Bench repository states no license of its own; its README asks that decrypted
  tasks and rubrics are never published or used for training, and this repository keeps run data
  out of version control.
